---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

const post = {
 title: 'Nevada OSHA Heat Rules 2026: Workwear Planning for Las Vegas Contractors',
 description:
 'A practical workwear planning guide for Nevada heat exposure. Start with the employer job hazard analysis, current Nevada OSHA guidance, and product documentation.',
 category: 'Compliance',
 readTime: '9 min read',
 date: 'Apr 27, 2026',
 isoDate: '2026-04-27',
 image: '/images/generated/workwear-flatlay.jpg',
 imageAlt: 'Breathable workwear options prepared for employer review in Las Vegas',
 slug: 'nevada-osha-heat-rules-2026-workwear',
}

const faqs = [
 {
  q: 'What does the Nevada heat illness regulation require?',
  a: 'Nevada Regulation R131-24 requires covered employers to assess working conditions that may cause occupational heat illness. Covered employers must address identified hazards in their written safety program. Use current Nevada OSHA guidance for the complete requirements.',
 },
 {
  q: 'Does Nevada OSHA require a specific work shirt?',
  a: 'The regulation does not prescribe one universal shirt. Clothing and PPE are factors in the job hazard analysis. The employer selects controls and products for the actual task, environment, and other hazards.',
 },
 {
  q: 'Can lightweight clothing replace other required PPE?',
  a: 'No. Heat planning does not remove requirements identified for traffic, electrical, chemical, fall, or other hazards. The employer and safety lead must review the complete protective system.',
 },
 {
  q: 'Can Bighorn Threads certify heat-rule compliance?',
  a: 'No. Bighorn can quote apparel options and request available product documents. The employer remains responsible for its hazard analysis, safety program, training, controls, and product approval.',
 },
]

const schema = {
 '@context': 'https://schema.org',
 '@graph': [
  {
   '@type': 'Article',
   headline: post.title,
   description: post.description,
   image: `https://bighornthreads.com${post.image}`,
   datePublished: post.isoDate,
   dateModified: '2026-08-21',
   author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Bighorn Threads', url: 'https://bighornthreads.com/about/' },
   publisher: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'Bighorn Threads',
    logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://bighornthreads.com/images/logos/bighorn-logo-color.png' },
   },
   mainEntityOfPage: `https://bighornthreads.com/blog/${post.slug}/`,
  },
  {
   '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
   itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://bighornthreads.com/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Blog', item: 'https://bighornthreads.com/blog/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: post.title, item: `https://bighornthreads.com/blog/${post.slug}/` },
   ],
  },
  {
   '@type': 'FAQPage',
   mainEntity: faqs.map((faq) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: faq.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: faq.a },
   })),
  },
 ],
}
---

<BaseLayout
 title={post.title}
 description={post.description}
 canonical={`https://bighornthreads.com/blog/${post.slug}/`}
 ogImage={post.image}
 type="article"
 publishedDate={post.isoDate}
>
 <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />

 <article class="bg-concrete">
  <header class="border-b border-hairline bg-paper">
   <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pt-16 pb-12 sm:px-6 sm:pt-20 lg:px-8">
    <nav class="mb-6 font-mono text-xs text-ash" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
     <a href="/" class="hover:text-gold-600">Home</a><span class="px-2">/</span><a href="/blog/" class="hover:text-gold-600">Blog</a>
    </nav>
    <span class="kicker mb-3">{post.category}</span>
    <h1 class="mb-6 font-heading text-3xl font-extrabold uppercase leading-tight tracking-tight text-charcoal sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl">{post.title}</h1>
    <p class="mb-8 text-xl leading-relaxed text-ash">Use current Nevada OSHA guidance and your job hazard analysis to evaluate clothing and PPE for heat exposure.</p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2 border-t border-hairline pt-6 font-mono text-sm text-ash">
     <span class="text-gold-600">Bighorn Threads Team</span><span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span>{post.readTime}</span><span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><time datetime={post.isoDate}>{post.date}</time>
    </div>
   </div>
  </header>

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 pt-10 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
   <img src={post.image} alt={post.imageAlt} width="1200" height="675" loading="eager" class="w-full border border-hairline object-cover" />
  </div>

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
   <aside class="mb-10 border border-hairline bg-panel p-7">
    <p class="mb-3 font-mono text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gold-600">Quick Answer</p>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal sm:text-xl">Workwear is one input in heat-risk planning. The employer must evaluate the task, weather, workload, duration, radiant heat, air movement, protective clothing, and other PPE. No shirt can certify compliance by itself.</p>
   </aside>

   <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Nevada approved Regulation R131-24 in 2024. Nevada OSHA's official guidance says covered employers must perform a written job hazard analysis for occupational heat exposure. The analysis must be reviewed when a job task materially changes.</p>
   <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">The regulation and guidance control. This article is educational and is not legal, medical, or safety advice.</p>

   <h2 id="official-sources" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">Start With Current Nevada OSHA Sources</h2>
   <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Read the <a href="https://www.leg.state.nv.us/Register/2024Register/R131-24AP.pdf" rel="noopener" target="_blank" class="text-gold-700 underline hover:text-gold-600">approved regulation</a> and <a href="https://dir.nv.gov/uploadedFiles/dirnvgov/content/OSHA/Guidance/2025-01-29%20%28Heat%20Illness%20Prevention%20Guidance%29.pdf" rel="noopener" target="_blank" class="text-gold-700 underline hover:text-gold-600">Nevada OSHA guidance</a>. Check the <a href="https://dir.nv.gov/OSHA/Home/" rel="noopener" target="_blank" class="text-gold-700 underline hover:text-gold-600">Nevada OSHA home page</a> for updates.</p>
   <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">The official materials distinguish required actions from recommended practices. They also explain coverage, written safety program duties, training, emergency response, and climate-controlled exemptions.</p>

   <h2 id="hazard-analysis" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">Connect Apparel to the Job Hazard Analysis</h2>
   <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Do not choose a summer uniform from temperature alone. Document the actual job and all required protection.</p>
   <ul class="mb-8 ml-6 list-disc space-y-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
    <li><strong>Work conditions.</strong> Review air temperature, humidity, radiant and conductive heat, air movement, workload, and exposure duration.</li>
    <li><strong>Protective system.</strong> Include required high-visibility, arc-rated, flame-resistant, chemical, cut, and other PPE.</li>
    <li><strong>Garment documents.</strong> Compare product labels, fabric details, care instructions, and manufacturer data.</li>
    <li><strong>Worker factors.</strong> Follow the employer's program for training, communication, acclimatization, monitoring, and emergency response.</li>
   </ul>

   <h2 id="workwear-review" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">Questions to Ask Before Ordering Workwear</h2>
   <ul class="mb-8 ml-6 list-disc space-y-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
    <li>Which hazards and project rules apply to each role?</li>
    <li>Which garment classifications and manufacturer documents are required?</li>
    <li>How do fabric weight, construction, color, ventilation, fit, and layering affect the complete program?</li>
    <li>Will decoration add ink, thread, backing, heat, or covered area that needs manufacturer review?</li>
    <li>Are every product, size, substitution, price, and delivery term confirmed in writing?</li>
   </ul>

   <h2 id="hi-vis-fr" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">Heat Planning With Hi-Vis and FR Requirements</h2>
   <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Heat exposure does not cancel another identified hazard. If the employer requires high-visibility or arc-rated apparel, evaluate products within that approved category.</p>
   <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Review the exact product with the employer, safety lead, and manufacturer. Do not infer a garment's class, arc rating, or suitability from color, fabric weight, or marketing language.</p>
   <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Decoration can affect a protective garment. Obtain written approval for thread, backing, ink, curing, size, and placement before production.</p>

   <h2 id="quote" class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">What Bighorn Can Put in a Quote</h2>
   <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Bighorn can coordinate product options through selected production partners. A proposal can identify the exact garments, available product documents, decoration plan, quantities, pricing, and expected timing.</p>
   <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">Availability, substitutions, freight, documentation, and production terms depend on the selected partner. Your employer and safety lead approve the final product.</p>

   <section class="mt-12 border border-hairline bg-panel p-8">
    <h2 class="mb-3 font-heading text-2xl font-extrabold uppercase tracking-tight text-charcoal">Review workwear options for your heat plan</h2>
    <p class="mb-6 text-lg text-ash">Send the crew roles, work environment, required PPE, quantities, and current garment list. We will build a written proposal for employer review.</p>
    <a href="/contact/" class="btn-primary text-base">Request a Workwear Review</a>
   </section>

   <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="mb-6 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="space-y-5">
     {faqs.map((faq) => (
      <div class="border border-hairline bg-paper p-6">
       <h3 class="mb-2 font-heading text-xl font-bold text-charcoal">{faq.q}</h3>
       <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-ash">{faq.a}</p>
      </div>
     ))}
    </div>
   </section>
  </div>
 </article>
</BaseLayout>
